  "details": "Note: This feedback is a combination of my friends opinion and my observation watching them.\nThey tried out the new IK in full body last night, and were primarily laying down. \nFrom their experience, when they loaded into a VR Chat word, the white balls that dictate where the trackers are on ones avatar moved from where they actually were, to where VR Chat -thought- they were. They literally watched this transition happen. They noted that it was as if it was trying to move the balls into a position of an avatar bigger than what they were in.\nThey can no longer get into a comfortable looking sitting position now the way they did with the old IK. Certain joints that used to move properly with them no longer do. (Example: Their knees would not move properly with them when they moved them. Their knees were not in the position they were IRL. This was not an issue in the old IK.)\nThey noted they could possibly see how these changes could benefit standing/walking, but are severely hurting laying position full body.",
